WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.850
Let’s work one.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.950
Follow the diagram.

3
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.775
At nine hundred, you’re steering zero nine zero true at twelve knots.

4
00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:11.650
A light bears zero two zero true.

5
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.600
Plot that line.

6
00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:17.775
At nine thirty, the same light bears three three zero true.

7
00:00:18.025 --> 00:00:19.925
Plot the second line.

8
00:00:20.175 --> 00:00:22.650
How far did you run between them?

9
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.175
Thirty minutes at twelve knots.

10
00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:28.325
Six miles, along zero nine zero.

11
00:00:28.575 --> 00:00:30.800
Now advance the first line.

12
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.850
Pick any point on the nine hundred line.

13
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.275
Measure six miles from it in the direction zero nine zero.

14
00:00:38.525 --> 00:00:42.975
Through that new point, draw a line parallel to the nine hundred line.

15
00:00:43.225 --> 00:00:45.050
Why does any point work?

16
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:50.700
Because you’re moving the whole line, and every point on it moves the same way.

17
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:56.550
Where the advanced line crosses the nine thirty line is your nine thirty running fix.

18
00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.675
Label it R fix.
